    "body": "## Summary\n\n**Revert PR #275 (ADR-070)** — the ADR-070 font-weight/font-style pipeline passed all 8 fixture checks but regressed Wikipedia rendering: **section headings became invisible** (blank bands where `History`, `HTML5`, `Elements` should render).\n\n**Root cause hypothesis (unverified, deferred to next session):** Wikipedia's `<h2>` elements use `font-family: 'Linux Libertine', 'Georgia', 'Times', serif`. Before ADR-070, Pango resolved this as regular weight and fell back to a working serif. After ADR-070, Pango requests **bold** \"Linux Libertine\" and fails fontconfig resolution, producing a zero-size layout → invisible text. The fixture passed because it used default `Sans` (well-installed, has bold variant).\n\n**Diagnosis plan for next session:**\n1. Reproduce on branch `feat/adr-070-preserve` (recreatable via `git branch feat/adr-070-preserve 6d3e61d`)\n2. Run 5-heading fixture (`docs/adr070-diagnostic.html`) — isolates font-family resolution vs cascade specificity vs wrapper structure\n3. Likely fix: strip quotes/commas from `font-family` before `pango_font_description_set_family` — `'Linux Libertine', 'Georgia', 'Times', serif` should become `Linux Libertine` (first token, unquoted)\n\n## What this PR does\n\nReverts merge commit `6d3e61d` (PR #275), backing out both commits:\n- `4d0ce3d` — `chore(diagnostic): DUMP-DOM layout tree stats + ADR-070 spec` (**KEPT** — see below)\n- `0718cd3` — `feat(render): font weight + font style pipeline (ADR-070)` (reverted)\n\n**The diagnostic + spec are preserved** — the revert only touches the implementation. `docs/decisions/070-font-weight-style.md` remains on main with status \"Implemented\" but with a note that implementation was reverted pending font-resolution fix. `RenderPipeline::dump_layout_stats()` remains available via `HONEYBEE_DUMP_DOM=1`.\n\n**Also adds back `docs/adr070-fidelity-test.html`** (was deleted by the revert) so next-session diagnosis has the fixture available.\n\n## Preserves\n\n- **ADR-069** (viewport-clipped paint) — untouched\n- **ADR-068** (Cairo workaround) — untouched\n- **ADR-067** (JPEG decode) — untouched\n- 691 / 2641 tests pass\n- Wikipedia renders with **visible, flat headings** (restored pre-ADR-070 state)\n\n## Why this is the right call\n\nMain safety is the invariant. Shipping ADR-069 (architectural win, verified) alone is safer than ADR-069 + ADR-070 with a Wikipedia regression. Fixture-passed does not mean Wikipedia-passed; ADR-070 hit exactly the failure mode fixture-only verification can't catch. Revert now, diagnose cleanly off main next session.\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Post-revert visual**: Wikipedia headings visible again (flat, not bold). All prior ADRs intact.\n\nRefs #275\n",
